// Shape: transitive closure, bound query.
//
// Provenance: canonical magic-sets example. Beeri & Ramakrishnan, "On the
// Power of Magic", PODS 1987 -- transitive closure with a bound source
// argument is their running example throughout the paper. Also
// OpenRuleBench's "datalog_recursion" category, test name
// "transitive_closure" (Liang, Fodor, Wan, Kifer, WWW 2009) -- same
// shape, independent citation.
//
// No negation in this shape; it exists in the family as the positive-
// fragment baseline (T_none/T_souffle only, no E_recoverable) rather than
// to test the guard.
//
// Fixture: harness/fixtures_lib.py's gen_core_rest_graph (controllable
// reachable-set size, the P1/Phase-0.5 lesson).

.decl edge(a:number, b:number)
.input edge

.decl tc(a:number, b:number)
tc(x,y) :- edge(x,y).
tc(x,y) :- tc(x,z), edge(z,y).

.decl q_tc(y:number)
.output q_tc
q_tc(y) :- tc(1,y).
